# Extra skips for the MULTISHARD sweep (shards>1), used IN ADDITION to
# valkey-sync.skip by sweep-shards.sh. Kinds:
#
#  (A) cluster-incompatible tests — CORRECT dreads behavior under sharding, the
#      Valkey unit suite just isn't cluster-aware. A multi-key op whose keys land
#      on different slots gets -CROSSSLOT (Redis Cluster's contract); the test
#      used arbitrary keys and didn't hashtag. Not a bug — a conscious decision.
#  (B) commands forbidden under sharding by design (SWAPDB — the db spans all
#      shards, cross-shard atomicity too costly for a rare admin op).
#  (E) MULTI/EXEC/WATCH under sharding (v1 gap; un-skip when same-slot MULTI
#      ships to the owner as a unit).
#  (F) not sharding: fails identically at shards=1 (suite drift / old gaps).
#  [(C) cross-shard pub/sub and (D) INFO/stats aggregation LANDED — phase 2.5c;
#   their former skips are gone.]
#
# NOTE: commands dreads does NOT support at all are a global matter, not a
# sharding one, and live in valkey-sync.skip — not here. See SHARDING-COMMANDS.md.
#
# Matching (tests/support/test.tcl search_pattern_list): a line whose FIRST char
# is `/` is a regexp (unanchored substring); the leading `/` is stripped but a
# trailing `/` is NOT — so write `/pattern`, never `/pattern/`. Any other line is
# an exact full-name match. Test names may carry a `{$type}` prefix (e.g.
# "{standalone} SCAN ...") — use the regexp form to match through it.

# (A) CROSSSLOT — multi-key ops across slots (test must hashtag to co-locate).
# NB: the "COPY basic usage for <type>" tests DO co-locate (mykey{t}/mynewkey{t})
# and pass — do not skip them; only genuinely cross-slot multi-key ops go here.
MSETEX with illegal arguments
Untagged multi-key commands
# untagged `r del myzset myzset2 myzset3` at the top (upstream {cluster:skip});
# the raw error aborts the whole file, so skipping is load-bearing
BZMPOP should not blocks on non key arguments - #10762

# (A/DEBUG) DEBUG OBJECT/JMAP on a specific key isn't routed under sharding
# (DEBUG is test/dev infra with a local executeCommand handler, no hop).
INCR can modify objects in-place

# (B) forbidden under sharding by design
/SWAPDB

# (E) MULTI/EXEC/WATCH under sharding — documented v1 gap (SHARDING.md "out of
# scope"): EXEC hops its commands one at a time (yielding at each flush), so a
# transaction is NOT atomic even same-slot (an owner-parked blocked client can
# wake MID-transaction), queued blocking commands serve the router's local
# keyspace, and the WATCH epoch is per-shard. Un-skip when same-slot MULTI
# ships to the owner as a unit (phase 2.5c candidate).
BRPOPLPUSH inside a transaction
BLPOP inside a transaction
BLMPOP_LEFT inside a transaction
PUSH resulting from BRPOPLPUSH affect WATCH
BZPOPMIN unblock but the key is expired and then block again - reprocessing command
BLPOP unblock but the key is expired and then block again - reprocessing command
# also (D)-flavored: asserts `r client list` sees a conn on ANOTHER router
# (CLIENT LIST is per-router); its fail path has a harness bug ($cmd undefined)
# that ABORTS the file, so skipping is load-bearing
BRPOPLPUSH does not affect WATCH while still blocked

# (F) NOT sharding: fail identically at shards=1 (valkey-9.1.0 suite drift,
# tracked in the main blackbox TODO). Skipped here so the multishard sweep's
# verdict flags only sharding gaps.
List listpack -> quicklist encoding conversion
List encoding conversion when RDB loading
# hangs 300s: background active-expire never fires the `expired` notification
# on db 9 (fails identically at shards=1; pre-existing, NOT a sharding gap)
Keyspace notifications: expired events (background expire)
